bug_report:
[13 Regression] forwprop -fwrapv miscompilation
The function f below returns an incorrect result for INT_MIN when compiled with -O1 -fwrapv for X86_64:


__attribute__((noipa)) int f(int x) {
    int w = (x >= 0 ? x : 0);
    int y = -x;
    int z = (y >= 0 ? y : 0);
    return w + z;
}

int
main ()
{
  if (f(0x80000000) != 0)
    __builtin_abort ();
  return 0;
}


What is happening is that forwprop has optimized

  w_2 = MAX_EXPR <x_1(D), 0>;
  y_3 = -x_1(D);
  z_4 = MAX_EXPR <y_3, 0>;
  _5 = w_2 + z_4;
  return _5;

to

  _5 = ABS_EXPR <x_1(D)>;
  return _5;
